From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: retroforge <retroforge@invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:20:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(LibraryDesktop): a Steam shortcut starts Steam's gamepad
 UI, as the Steam plugin does

Steam writes a desktop shortcut for each game it installs
(~/.local/share/applications/<Game>.desktop, Exec=steam
steam://rungameid/<id>), and OGUI's desktop library lists it. Its quirk
for those shortcuts added '-silent' only: the line with the Steam
plugin's flags is there, commented out. Without -gamepadui, Steam
started in its desktop mode, and a game launched from the library came
up behind a sign-in window, the desktop library and a "Launching..."
dialog that stayed in front for as long as the launch took (HW, KONKR
Pocket FIT, 2026-10-21: Hades; the shortcut's launch item shares the
game's card with the other library's and was the one used).

The quirk now adds what the Steam plugin passes: -gamepadui -steamos3
-steampal -steamdeck -silent.

---
 core/systems/library/library_desktop.gd | 9 +++++----
 1 file changed

--- a/core/systems/library/library_desktop.gd
+++ b/core/systems/library/library_desktop.gd
@@ -91,10 +91,11 @@
 	if not _contains_string(launch_item.args, "steam://rungameid"):
 		return
 		
-	# If the desktop shortcut is for Steam, add the '-silent' argument so it
-	# doesn't launch into the Steam interface
-	#var args := PackedStringArray(["-gamepadui", "-steamos3", "-steampal", "-steamdeck", "-silent"])
-	var args := PackedStringArray(["-silent"])
+	# If the desktop shortcut is for Steam, start Steam as the Steam plugin
+	# does: its gamepad UI, silent. With '-silent' alone Steam came up in its
+	# desktop mode over the game: a sign-in window, the desktop library and a
+	# "Launching..." dialog, for as long as the game took to start.
+	var args := PackedStringArray(["-gamepadui", "-steamos3", "-steampal", "-steamdeck", "-silent"])
 	args.append_array(launch_item.args)
 	launch_item.args = args
 
